@@ -122,3 +122,35 @@ bare `patch["id"] in text` substring. A patch ID merely named in the
 file-header banner or the generator's own header WARNING block can no
 longer register as reached. It accepts a `COMPOSE_REGISTRY` profile name
 **or** an arbitrary absolute path to a compose file.
+
+## `chat_template` wiring is source-aware (follow-up to #1597 / #1610)
+
+`delivery_mechanism: chat_template` patches are judged on the
+`compose_effective_text` merged body (real `extends:` semantics) and must
+satisfy BOTH halves of their wiring, neither of which is satisfied by the
+bare `--chat-template` flag that half the template-mounting composes pass
+for some *other* patch's template:
+
+- **the mount is this patch's** — the bind-mount line must carry the
+  vendored template's own directory or filename (`qwen38-reasoning-effort-template/…`,
+  `apex-qwen-chat-template.jinja`, `glm53-minja-numeric-index/…`) next to the
+  declared `mounted_at`, exactly as #1610 required for install scripts. A
+  bare `mounted_at` is not identifying: `qwen38-reasoning-effort-template`
+  declares the *suffix* `/chat_template.jinja` (it mounts over each model
+  dir's own template), so that string appears on every other template's
+  mount line too. A line that passes the engine flag is the flag's
+  argument, never a mount.
+- **the flag names the mounted path** — `--chat-template` (vLLM) or
+  `--chat-template-file` (llama.cpp) matched with a word boundary, on the
+  flag's own line or the adjacent list item. `--chat-template` is a
+  substring of `--chat-template-file`, so a llama.cpp compose does not
+  satisfy a vLLM-style invoke.
+
+A template mounted **over** the served checkpoint's own
+`chat_template.jinja` (`/chat_template.jinja`,
+`/models/<weights>/chat_template.jinja`, carnice's
+`…/carnice-v2-…/chat_template.jinja`) is auto-loaded by the engine, so the
+mount alone is load-bearing there and no flag is required; a standalone
+`/etc/*.jinja` target is only selectable through the flag, so the flag is
+required. `wired_at: [volumes, command]` and `[volumes, entrypoint]` are
+the same insertion point and are treated identically.
