+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# chat_template negative controls — the bare `--chat-template` flag is shared by
+# EVERY template-mounting compose (and is a substring of `--chat-template-file`),
+# so a flag alone, or a mount of SOME OTHER patch's template, must never count
+# as wiring for a chat_template patch.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+_ct = {p["id"]: p for p in chat_template_patches}
+# (a) The Qwen3.8 reasoning-effort template mounts over each model dir's own
+#     chat_template.jinja, so its `mounted_at` (/chat_template.jinja) is a
+#     SUFFIX of every other template's mount line. It must NOT reach a Gemma
+#     compose, whose own canonical template is a different vendored file.
+# (b) apex / glm53 are wired with llama.cpp's --chat-template-file; a vLLM
+#     compose that passes --chat-template for ITS OWN template mounts neither.
+for _pid, _other in (
